From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:18:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics-tcm: Enable analog supply before digital
 supply

Enable AVDD and VDD sequentially while reset remains asserted. The bulk
regulator helper enables asynchronously, so array order does not fix
supply order. Follow the order in tegu's syna_gtd driver; a failure of
the bulk-enable version has not been established.

Tegu builds syna_gtd, whose syna_spi_enable_regulator() enables avdd
before vdd. Its board DT declares synaptics,power-delay-ms = <200>.
Retain that declared 200 ms settling policy here. At the linked vendor
revision the general power_delay_ms sleep is commented out, so the DT
value is not proof of an active vendor wait or a minimum hardware delay.

Pantah instead builds syna_c10: vdd first, then avdd, followed by its
power-on delay. The cheetah DT also declares 200 ms. Its mainline node
has no supplies, so both requests are dummies today. Once those rails
are described, this driver's analog-first order will differ from stock;
it is not established as the required order for every supported board.

This changes neither the TouchComm v1 protocol nor the SPI host. The
sequential sequence supplies physical input on the private Pixel 9a
bring-up kernel; regulator selectors and firmware remain unchanged.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/tegu/+/6276884d9940694b25a6934671918ec8ac412ee8/BUILD.bazel
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/touch/synaptics_touch/+/a5d225cc4034f3e98c6f7f0c0c7e182c254a517f/syna_gtd/syna_tcm2_platform_spi.c
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/tegu/+/6276884d9940694b25a6934671918ec8ac412ee8/dts/zuma-tegu-common-touch.dtsi
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/pantah/+/9810b5840267f30cd3cc81d6b054de313140af58/BUILD.bazel
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/touch/synaptics_touch/+/a5d225cc4034f3e98c6f7f0c0c7e182c254a517f/syna_c10/syna_tcm2_platform_spi.c
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/devices/google/pantah/+/9810b5840267f30cd3cc81d6b054de313140af58/dts/gs201-cheetah-touch.dtsi
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c
index 10395a7c7..53ac4287a 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm.c
@@ -753,7 +753,6 @@ static int tcm_input_init(struct tcm_ts *ts)
 
 static int tcm_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
 {
-	static const char * const supplies[] = { "vdd", "avdd" };
 	struct device *dev = &spi->dev;
 	struct tcm_ts *ts;
 	int error;
@@ -786,11 +785,14 @@ static int tcm_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(ts->reset_gpio),
 				     "failed to get reset GPIO\n");
 
-	error = devm_regulator_bulk_get_enable(dev, ARRAY_SIZE(supplies),
-					       supplies);
+	/* Keep the analog rail ahead of the digital rail, as at cold startup. */
+	error = devm_regulator_get_enable(dev, "avdd");
 	if (error)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, error, "failed to enable supplies\n");
-	msleep(20);
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, error, "failed to enable analog supply\n");
+	error = devm_regulator_get_enable(dev, "vdd");
+	if (error)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, error, "failed to enable digital supply\n");
+	msleep(200);
 
 	error = devm_request_threaded_irq(dev, spi->irq, NULL, tcm_irq,
 					  IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_NO_AUTOEN,
